      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Fancy this is a bit more open than the market would suggest. JIMMY THE BEAR (1) won well here three back when swooping down the outside before two even efforts at Flemington. He meets the winner 3kg better from last time and does go particularly well here as well. SEAFALL (5) raced wide and dropped out in the Winter Final last time but had won a key lead-up prior which has her firmly in the mix. Williams should give her every hope from the inside gate. ST LAWRENCE (7) looks ready to win. He's been slowly building this time in and got home very well here over 1400m last time off a slow speed. Now gets to a mile and looks set to peak. FIRST CHORUS (9) is the 'weights' horse, dropping to 51.5kg after the claim. She won well last time although this is a fair step up and the early quote looks skinny. DETONATOR JACK (2) was a shock winner of the Winter Final last time. Not sure what to do with him but away from Flemington is possibly a knock.",
